# Build-context exclusions for the server image (`Dockerfile`).
#
# WHY THIS IS A BUILD-TIME FILE, NOT A SIZE OPTIMISATION: `Dockerfile` does
# `COPY . .`, so the whole context is sent to the daemon and then walked on every
# build. A working checkout carries a local virtualenv — a ~200 MB tree of
# macOS/arm64 binaries that the image can never use, because it installs its own
# dependencies for Linux — plus test and tool caches that are regenerated on the
# other side. Excluding them is the difference between a context that uploads in
# a second and one that uploads for a minute before any layer is built.
#
# Everything below is build weight or host contamination, never source. Keep it
# to that bar: an entry that removes something the build reads turns a slow
# build into a broken one.

# Existing entries, unchanged. `tests` in particular is left exactly as it was:
# this image serves the HTTP API and does not run the suite, but the ignore file
# is shared ground with the probe image's own context rules
# (`scripts/xplat/Dockerfile.probe.dockerignore` deliberately does NOT ignore
# `tests/`, because the probe boots the TUI against the app double that lives
# there).
.github
examples
tests

# Local virtualenvs and interpreter droppings.
.venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.egg-info

# Test and tool caches: regenerated by whatever runs them.
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# Sibling checkouts and JS dependencies.
.worktrees
node_modules
